---
import { BleedImage, Slide } from '@decks';

import figmaArchitecture from '../images/figma-architecture.png?url';

// The design half of "distributed and consumed", paired with
// 3-Architecture.astro. That one is how the code shipped; this one is how
// the design side was structured. Decisions spoken over the artwork.
//
// Replaced the button-variants screenshot, which showed what the system
// looked like rather than how it was built, and the panel asked for less
// of that. The token pipeline is the actual decision: one base set
// forking into light and dark semantics, recombining into component
// tokens, then out to three platforms.
//
// Source is 1291x1009, aspect 1.2795, much squarer than the screenshot it
// replaced. Scaled to 1126x880 so the aspect matches exactly and
// object-cover crops nothing, bled off the bottom like slide 3 so the two
// architecture slides sit identically. The diagram's own bottom margin
// absorbs the bleed, so its content ends around y=1011.
//
// The three platforms here are the same three counted on 2-Impact.astro.
---

<Slide subtitle="Figma Architecture">
	<BleedImage
		src={figmaArchitecture}
		alt="Figma token architecture. Base tokens feed separate light and dark theme semantic tokens, which both feed component tokens, which in turn feed the Web, iOS, and Android component sets."
		bleed="bottom"
		class="h-[880px] w-[1126px] object-cover"
	/>
</Slide>
